## 7. Random Module

The `random` module is useful for creating simulated data when real measurements are not available.

### Random Integer

```python
random.randint(1, 6)
```

Generates a random integer from **1 to 6**.

### Random Decimal

```python
random.uniform(24.90, 25.10)
```

Generates a random decimal value between the given limits.

This can be used to simulate **shaft diameter measurements**.

